37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"- **Kenji**: The glasshouses are booked solid for two more cycles, and the spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The incident logs confirm the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks. The portfolio review shows breeding-based projects overrun twice as often.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The closeout files confirm catalogue awards still draw users a decade later, while mechanism-focused ones ended unresolved.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: The closeout files confirm catalogue awards still draw users a decade later, while mechanism-focused ones ended unresolved.""}]}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, free computing is a blessing. @Kenji, idle spectroscopy is a tragedy. We must value the hands that keep the lights on.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, the free computing is a relief, but the rising animal-unit day rates are a heavy burden for the awardee.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that idle spectroscopy suite is a nightmare. If we pick a project needing it, we’re gambling on a broken system.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. That idle time is pure waste. I’m checking the portfolio review to see if these interruptions correlate with specific project types.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
